#
# A box nobody has made into a mesh node yet behaves like an ordinary router.
#
# Measured 2026-08-17 on the first production image, on a freshly flashed card
# that had been through nothing but firstboot:
#
#     radio0/1/2   disabled='0'        all three on
#     wifi-iface   2, and that is all there is
#       ap_mld_1   'OpenWrt-'          on the air
#       ap_mld_2   'MAP--BH'           on the air   <- the mesh backhaul
#
# The default networks the board is supposed to come up with are not
# overwritten - they are simply not there, replaced by two sections nobody
# asked for. Petr put it plainly: without doing anything, and perhaps never
# wanting a mesh at all, the user loses the networks that belong there and
# gains a backhaul they did not order.
#
# It happens because the image ships mapcontroller.enabled=1 AND
# mapagent.enabled=1, so both daemons start on a box with no role, and
# map-agent builds its BSSes from its own factory sections. Broadcasting the
# backhaul before onboarding is also what project_easymesh_wired_onboarding
# warns against: existing nodes can hang themselves on the newcomer and form a
# loop, and the only thing preventing it today is that the factory key differs.
#
# The mark is /etc/mapc/role, written by easymesh-role before it touches anything
# else, or /etc/easymesh-wps-pending while a join is in flight. Nodes configured
# before the marker existed get it from 88-easymesh-role-marker, which runs just
# before this file. The same two tests gate 11-multiap-genconfig and
# 991-multiap-genconfig; if one changes, all three change.
#
# ⚠️ Two earlier versions of this test were wrong, both for the same reason - they
# asked about a value the factory also writes.
#
# The first tested mapagent.@controller_select[0]. The factory ships that section,
# so this script exited at its first line on every boot and was dead from the day
# it shipped.
#
# The second added a non-empty dhcp.lan.ignore, on the belief that only
# easymesh-role writes it. easymesh-dhcp-safe writes it too, on every box that is
# not a controller - factory ones included. That put the mark on an untouched
# router and reopened all three gates one boot later. Traced on hardware
# 2026-08-17; the board came up broadcasting a backhaul three builds running.
#
# 🔑 A mark only means "someone decided" if nothing but a decision can produce it.
#
# Neither way in is affected. The over-the-air join builds its own STA section
# (wireless.wps_join on radio1) and only reads map-agent's config, so it does
# not need the daemon; the cable join runs easymesh-role, which switches both
# daemons on and reboots into a configured node.
#
# A box that has already taken a role keeps the section through sysupgrade with
# keep-config, so this never disturbs a working mesh. After firstboot the
# section is gone with the rest of the overlay - and then it should apply,
# because that box is factory-fresh again by definition.

# The same test as everywhere else, from the same code. This file used to keep
# its own inline copy, which meant a failure in 88 turned "we could not decide"
# into "factory" here - and this script's answer to factory is to switch both
# daemons off, on a node that may be carrying traffic. Three gates on three
# private copies of the mark is how the last four rounds of this bug happened.
[ -r /usr/share/easymesh/boot-window.sh ] || {
	echo "89-easymesh-quiet-until-role: cannot read boot-window.sh - leaving daemons alone" >&2
	exit 1
}
. /usr/share/easymesh/boot-window.sh

if is_mesh_node; then
	exit 0
fi

# Nothing to quiet down before map-agent has written its config at all. Exit
# non-zero so the file survives and runs again at the next boot, by which time
# it exists - the same reason 90-easymesh-mld-backhaul does it.
uci -q get mapagent >/dev/null 2>&1 || {
	echo "89-easymesh-quiet-until-role: no mapagent config yet, will retry at boot" >&2
	exit 1
}

changed=0
[ "$(uci -q get mapagent.agent.enabled)" = "0" ] || {
	uci set mapagent.agent.enabled='0'
	uci commit mapagent
	changed=1
}
[ "$(uci -q get mapcontroller.controller.enabled)" = "0" ] || {
	uci set mapcontroller.controller.enabled='0'
	uci commit mapcontroller
	changed=1
}

[ "$changed" = 1 ] && logger -t easymesh-config \
	"no mesh role yet - map-agent and map-controller left off, so the box does not put a backhaul on the air before anyone asks for one"

exit 0
